# Swarm Delivery

Reference guide for the Holly swarm delivery model. The Orchestrator stays in
one window and dispatches bounded subagent workers — `runSubagent` on VS Code,
`Agent` on Claude Code, or `multi_agent_v1.spawn_agent` on Codex — that each do
one assigned issue, return a structured final report, and exit. This skill is
the operations manual for the `orchestrate-swarm` workflow. The cockpit
checklist lives in `orchestrator-v2.agent.md`; the routing summary lives in the
`orchestration` skill.

The machine-readable routing source of truth is
`src/holly/agents/swarm-agents.manifest.yaml`. The runtime/model strength map is
`src/holly/agents/model-capability-tiers.yaml`. Keep this skill aligned with
those files; they win on any numeric conflict.

---

## 0. Mode gate (single-agent vs multi-agent)

Swarm delivery requires `multi-agent` mode. Holly's operating mode is resolved by
`holly mode` (and shown in `holly status`): `multi-agent` allows sub-agent
dispatch; `single-agent` blocks it.

Before any dispatch, the Orchestrator checks the mode. In `single-agent` mode:

- Do NOT dispatch swarm workers. The PreToolUse hook hard-blocks
  `Agent`/`Task`/`runSubagent`, so dispatch will fail anyway.
- Deliver the work directly in the Orchestrator session, or ask the user to
  switch: `holly mode multi` (this session) or `holly mode multi --default`
  (project default).
- A dispatched worker that somehow starts in single-agent mode MUST refuse and
  report the coordination error rather than work around it.

The rest of this skill assumes `multi-agent` mode.

