## 2. The swarm agents and their envelopes

Pulled from `swarm-agents.manifest.yaml`:

| Agent | Capability tier | Min model strength | Fallback | Envelope |
|-------|-----------------|--------------------|----------|----------|
| **swarm-tiny-implementation** | `tiny_implementation` | any | allowed | <=2 files / <=120 changed lines |
| **swarm-standard-implementation** | `standard_implementation` | standard | allowed | <=4 files / <=250 changed lines |
| **swarm-senior-implementation** | `senior_implementation` | senior | NOT allowed (escalate) | <=8 files / <=600 changed lines; architecture/cross-cutting/migration with explicit scope |
| **swarm-ui-browser-implementation** | `ui_browser_implementation` | standard | allowed | <=4 files / <=250 changed lines; requires browser tool |
| **swarm-principal-implementation** | `principal_implementation` | principal | NOT allowed (escalate) | <=12 files / <=900 changed lines; hardest large-context work; needs Claude Fable 5 |
| **swarm-reviewer** | `standard_review` | standard | allowed | read-only; verdict only |
| **swarm-senior-reviewer** | `senior_review` | senior | NOT allowed (escalate) | read-only; verdict only |
| **swarm-principal-reviewer** | `principal_review` | principal | NOT allowed (escalate) | read-only; verdict only; highest-stakes; needs Claude Fable 5 |

All swarm agents have `close_permission: false` and `merge_permission: false`.
Implementation agents have `edit_permission: true`; both reviewers have
`edit_permission: false`.

swarm-ui-browser-implementation has browser-tool fallback rules: if the browser
tool is unavailable and visual proof is required, escalate; if visual proof is
not required, proceed with a limitation note.

