## 6. Reviewer gate protocol

Reviewers are strictly read-only (no edit tool). A reviewer returns exactly one
verdict:

| Verdict | Meaning |
|---------|---------|
| `approve` | Branch meets acceptance criteria and scope; safe to integrate |
| `changes-requested` | Specific blocking findings; send a bounded fix prompt back |
| `blocked` | Cannot complete review (missing evidence, broken branch) |
| `escalate` | Needs senior review or a user decision |

Reviewers NEVER patch, commit, close, or merge. Their report includes the
verdict, blocking findings, non-blocking findings, tests checked, scope
assessment, closure recommendation, and the model+runtime report fields.

Choose `swarm-reviewer` for normal scoped review and `swarm-senior-reviewer`
for high-risk, disputed, architectural, security-sensitive, data-sensitive,
migration, or cross-cutting work. If senior review is required and no
senior-capable model is available, escalate — never approve on an under-powered
model.

