## 7. Integration ownership

ONLY the Orchestrator integrates branches and closes issues. Implementation
agents push their task branch and stop — they do NOT run `holly task finish`,
do NOT merge to main, and do NOT close issues.

Integration discipline:

1. Use a dedicated integration worktree; never merge from the main checkout.
2. Pull latest `origin/main` before each integration batch.
3. Merge approved branches one at a time in dependency order; resolve conflicts
   deliberately.
4. Run child-level verification after each merge and wave-level gates after the
   wave merge.
5. Close a child only after its branch is merged, verification passes, and the
   reviewer verdict is `approve`.

