## 10. Failure and escalation rules

- If a subagent returns `blocked` or `failed`, triage the cause. Retry once with
  clearer instructions if it is prompt/scope ambiguity; otherwise escalate to a
  stronger implementation agent or ask the user.
- If review requests changes, send one bounded fix prompt back to the original
  implementation agent when safe. Escalate to senior review or the user if the
  fix would change architecture, scope, or dependencies.
- If senior review is required and no senior-capable model is available,
  escalate — do not approve on an under-powered model.
- If a ui-browser child needs visual proof and no browser tool is available,
  escalate rather than dispatch.
- If useful parallelism drops below 2 or the remaining work is a shared
  integration path, execute directly or with a single subagent rather than
  pretending it is still a swarm.

